@startuml j3-booking-and-call-back
!include c4-sequence.iuml
title J3 Booking and call-back
actor "Patient" as Patient <<person>>
box "In the patient's browser"
participant "Patient chat\n(chat.js,\ncallback-ask.js,\nsync.js)" as Chat <<container>>
participant "Rules engine\n(core.js)" as Core <<component>>
database "Browser storage\n(localStorage)" as LS <<store>>
end box
box "Vercel functions"
participant "api/tickets.js" as Tix <<container>>
end box
database "Postgres\n(Neon)" as Store <<store>>
box "In the staff browser"
participant "Staff page\n(staff/staff.js,\nsync.js)" as SP <<container>>
end box
actor "Staff" as Staff <<person>>

== The request ==
Patient -> Chat : types "I want to\nbook a check-up\ntomorrow at 5 pm"\nand presses Send
Chat -> Core : FD.answer(message,\nclinic file, language)
Core --> Chat : the booking reply\nwith the time asked\nfor, status\n"needs human"
note over Core, LS : The chat never books a slot;\nit passes the request to the team.
Chat -> Core : FD.addTicket\n(question, reply,\nrequested time,\ncall back)
Core -> LS : the ticket joins\nthis browser's tickets
Chat --> Patient : "Thank you. I have\npassed your request\nfor ... to our team";\nbelow it the form\n"So we can call you\nback (optional)"
opt the patient fills the call-back form
  Patient -> Chat : fills "Your name" and\n"Phone number"\nand presses Save
  Chat -> Core : FD.updateTicket\n(name, phone with\nits country code)
  Core -> LS : the ticket now holds\nthe name and the number
  Chat --> Patient : "Thank you, <name>.\nWe will call <phone>."
end
Chat -> Tix : sync.js: POST /api/tickets\n(the ticket, with\nthis browser's key)
Tix -> Store : the row in the table\ntickets is added,\nthen updated
== At the desk ==
Staff -> SP : opens /staff\nand enters\nthe desk code
SP -> Tix : sync.js: GET /api/tickets\n(with the desk code)
Tix --> SP : the tickets of\nevery device
SP --> Staff : the ticket under\n"To call back"\nwith the name,\nthe phone and\n"requested <time>"
note left of SP : without the desk code\nthe staff page shows this\nbrowser's tickets only
@enduml
